# Model pin matrix — full catalog (best ∩ appropriate)

**Goal:** For every job, pin the **strongest model that fits that job** — not blindly the most expensive, and not silently `-fast` / low-effort.

When launching `Task` / subagents, **always set `model`** unless the tool forbids it. Prefer explicit slugs from this file over unset/`null`.

User override wins: if the user names a model or says “en iyi / max / kalite”, bias **up**; if they say “ucuz / hızlı / maliyet”, bias **down**.

---

## 1. Effort tiers (suffix)

Use the highest effort that still fits latency/budget for the job.

| Suffix | When |
|--------|------|
| `minimal` / `none` | Tiny classification, trivial yes/no (Muse / GPT only) |
| `low` | Simple edits, short answers, low-stakes |
| `medium` | Default competent work; CI triage; mid features |
| `high` | **Default for serious Excelbase work** |
| `xhigh` | Hard multi-step, ambiguous product/architecture |
| `max` | Highest reasoning; rare — security, data integrity, OCR correctness crises |

**Fast variants** (`*-fast`): only when the user wants speed **and** the job is interactive UI driving or time-boxed swarm work. Fast ≈ higher $/token; not “better”. Do **not** use fast for architecture, security, OCR, auth, or merge-critical logic.

